                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6a513852-f2c1-4738-8a37-e1bd7750a4d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "dd0241ed-c38e-3eb3-a473-cd9b2c32b1f8",
                        "source_sense_id": "85b26b35-f248-333e-84d7-30cc636f17df",
                        "target_lang_word": "unchecked",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unchecked",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                        "entry_id": "8b4b8300-6512-3f7b-9c8a-e5f894b2e129",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unrestrained, not held back."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29fc1d72-396b-4e45-b199-6399a20b09f0",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "unchecked ambition"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5f38f5f-e743-4a82-bc05-c3ed41e4b304",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "unchecked power"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbb0d470-694d-4581-89cd-5099a68fa0e5",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "The Earth's a Theefe, / That feeds and breeds by a compoſture ſtolne / From gen'rall excrement: each thing's a Theefe. The Lawes, your curbe and whip, in their rough power / Ha's vncheck'd Theft."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b1cbff38-7f2e-4f3a-9533-2e42007a0384",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "O happy captain, that may'st houze / In quarter free, and uncheckt brouze / On teeming hedge, when purse is light, / Or on the wholsom sallat bite: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f7af6412-9b77-4eee-b170-eee63d78c02c",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "[…] For, whenever his Bounty is miſus'd, by being made to miniſter to our Luſts or any unlawful Paſſions, if he ſhall ſtill ſuffer us to go on in an uncheckt Courſe of Proſperity, That is what may Pleaſe Us, and we may be likely to think it God's Favour and Kindneſs to Us, which would really be one of his Greateſt Plagues."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87f01075-340c-4e1f-9f1c-ef08bc6f7786",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "The buſy candidates for power and fame / Have hopes, and fears, and wiſhes juſt the ſame; / Diſabled both to combat, or to fly, / Muſt hear all taunts, and hear without reply. / Uncheck'd on both, loud rabbles vent their rage, / As mongrels bay the lion in a cage."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66951340-c373-421a-ab25-a18da6fe4770",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "He ſeeks reſpect—but how to gain it? / Wit, ſocial mirth, could ne'er obtain it: / And laughter, where it reigns uncheck'd, / Diſcards and diſſipates respect."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f21fc48-86eb-420e-b969-236055c06e7f",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "Far spread the moorey ground a level scene / Bespread with rush and one eternal green / That never felt the rage of blundering plough / Through centurys wreathed springs blossoms on its brow / Still meeting plains that stretched them far away / In uncheckt shadows of green brown and grey / Unbounded freedom ruled the wandering scene / Nor fence of ownership crept in between / To hide the prospect of the following eye / Its only bondage was the circling sky […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e3ab7b8-dd8c-4136-b203-4ae6abf54c16",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "Then ceased I from my envying state, / And knew that aweless intellect / Hath power upon the ways of fate, / And works through time and space uncheckt."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98659b7a-2583-4d97-8fcc-c13b17bed55b",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "Beyond the damaged bridge over the river, the railway was left to the unchecked attention of nature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "219d9211-70fe-47d8-9f0a-03e314f7c1b3",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "[H]ow long we should study 'before' we act is not a scientific judgment but a value judgment, weighing the costs of any present investment to slow down the future climate change versus the costs of that change descending on us unchecked."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe92e385-b23c-463f-b8eb-803ca416f9be",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "Nothing in today's torture, rendition, spying, and indefinite detention policies suggests human nature has evolved since [James] Madison's day, or since the Church Committee some three decades ago. Wise restraint—not unchecked and unbounded license—still makes us safe and keeps us free."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33809b25-0cc8-4cdd-bde1-1839e5f8dc36",
                                                "sense_id": "d2877a79-4983-3b38-a58c-a4cc6c0fa77f",
                                                "text": "Coristine is one of a team of teenage and twentysomething software engineers, apparently conscripted by Musk in his largely unchecked war against bureaucracy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "644552b4-d79c-3b91-9f64-2db5373fe1b2",
                                        "entry_id": "8b4b8300-6512-3f7b-9c8a-e5f894b2e129",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Not examined for accuracy, efficiency, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d673c54b-d75a-4edd-a876-f230a4e0c2d3",
                                                "sense_id": "644552b4-d79c-3b91-9f64-2db5373fe1b2",
                                                "text": "unchecked writings"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "788be34c-6ff4-4288-9f09-710cf0a28f53",
                                                "sense_id": "644552b4-d79c-3b91-9f64-2db5373fe1b2",
                                                "text": "unchecked findings"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51ec66db-0bb0-476c-a0d1-5abb5f5cd643",
                                                "sense_id": "644552b4-d79c-3b91-9f64-2db5373fe1b2",
                                                "text": "Java exceptions fall into two categories, called checked and unchecked exceptions. When you call a method that throws a checked exception, the compiler checks that you don't ignore it. You must tell the compiler what you are going to do about the exception if it is ever thrown. […] On the other hand, the compiler does not require you to keep track of unchecked exceptions. […] A checked exception describes a problem that is likely to occur at times, no matter how careful you are. The unchecked exceptions, on the other hand, are your fault."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5dbbc841-0bda-3a20-a702-05c680ebff38",
                                        "entry_id": "8b4b8300-6512-3f7b-9c8a-e5f894b2e129",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a check box: not checked (ticked or enabled)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74cb9438-a772-4464-ae6d-c88482f0e78f",
                                                "sense_id": "5dbbc841-0bda-3a20-a702-05c680ebff38",
                                                "text": "This pseudocode is unambiguous if we know that the previous state of all the boxes is \"unchecked.\" Because we can't be sure of that in buggy code, a better model might be: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13023104-ef8f-4779-af92-108d12e7da74",
                                                "sense_id": "5dbbc841-0bda-3a20-a702-05c680ebff38",
                                                "text": "Check boxes are a handy way to enable users to select one or more options that are not mutually exclusive. […] By default, [Microsoft] Word displays boxes unchecked."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "18b24994-2755-3d82-aa4c-153d3024795c",
                                        "entry_id": "8b4b8300-6512-3f7b-9c8a-e5f894b2e129",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a square: part of only one entry (that is, across or down, but not both)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29d1bcd9-8dfb-4722-b35b-0ab3dea5f0f5",
                                                "sense_id": "18b24994-2755-3d82-aa4c-153d3024795c",
                                                "text": "If there are W#95;1 \"unchecked\" whites (that is, those which enter into the solution of one clue only), and W#95;2 \"checked\" whites (those which enter into the solution of two clues), then the mean word length will be (W#95;1#43;2W#95;2)#47;C, where C is the number of clues. […] Acceptable (if unwelcome) difficulties arise when the initial letters of words occupy unchecked squares, because no hint then derives from other clues as to how that word will start. In six consecutive crossword puzzles in The Times, 16 per cent of the words had unchecked initial letters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f65fe17e-10c1-488f-bc4e-8ce36a51d167",
                                                "sense_id": "18b24994-2755-3d82-aa4c-153d3024795c",
                                                "text": "On a crossword puzzle grid, you shouldn't encounter any unchecked squares – white squares that are used in an Across entry but not in a Down entry, or vice versa. If unchecked squares were allowed, that would make your life harder – you'd have only one opportunity to figure out what belongs in that square. Instead, you always get two chances to fill a square: by solving the Across clue or the Down clue."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
